    "material_change_rule": {
      "group": "envelope",
      "binding": "specified",
      "rule": "Material and grammar stay coherent across the whole building, including elevations not visible from the street: one wall material family per building, changing only at a real structural line and returning fully around every corner, never applied as a 'front-only' theme.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "status": "drafted",
      "note": "All three members converge on this independently and it is, in every case, framed as the family's central argument against the neo-eclectic production-builder default: new-classical's own diagnostic_tells list 'a brick wall with a genuine water table, belt course, and moulded cap, all returning around every corner' and names a veneer return under 24 in as forbidden (c05); new-urbanist-traditional's own hard constraint (c05) requires 'one regional stylistic vocabulary per building, applied to all elevations including alley and side' and forbids 'changing material at an outside corner'; modern-farmhouse-traditional's own defining_characteristics state 'no material changes at an outside corner' directly, and its own long description names 'material return failure' as exactly the neo-eclectic defect all three branches of this family are reacting against."
    },
