    "window_grouping_rule": {
      "group": "openings",
      "binding": "specified",
      "rule": "All window heads on a given storey align to a single datum. This is the one proportional discipline every branch of the family holds in common even where profile depth, code enforcement, and market economics otherwise diverge sharply.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "status": "drafted",
      "note": "Explicitly stated by two of the three members and structurally implied by the third: new-urbanist-traditional's own hard constraint (c04, 'all heads on a storey aligned to a single datum'); modern-farmhouse-traditional's own hard constraint (c03, heads 'shall align to one datum per storey'), which its own text calls out as 'a genuine advance over the preceding node [neo-eclectic]'; new-classical's own governing_logic derives every opening from one declared module, which forces single-datum alignment as a direct consequence even though the node states it structurally rather than as an explicit head-alignment rule."
    },
